<title>GERMANY: Deutz sells environment technology unit.</title>
<headline>Deutz sells environment technology unit.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering group Deutz AG said on Tuesday that Baker Hughes, a U.S. provider of goods and services to the oil, gas and process industries, would buy the environment technology unit of its KHD Humboldt Wedag AG division.</p>
<p>Deutz said Baker Hughes would pay 92 million marks for the unit, which had sales of 160 million marks in 1996 and 350 employees.</p>
<p>The deal has already been approved by German anti-trust authorities and takes effect retroactively to July 1.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 260976 150</p>
</text>
